7
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:44.000
Hyperinflation hit thirteen thousand percent in five years.

8
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.460
Napoleon happened. Not great. Weimar Germany (nineteen twenties).

9
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:57.100
Germany lost World War One, printed money to pay reparations, and achieved twenty-nine thousand five hundred percent inflation

10
00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:04.340
per month, which is a number that should make your brain hurt because it means a loaf of bread that cost one mark in January

11
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:12.270
cost billions by fall. People burned money for heat because paper was worth more as fuel than as currency.

12
00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:18.480
Hitler happened. Really not great. United States (nineteen seventeen to present).

13
00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:25.870
Created the Federal Reserve in nineteen thirteen. Immediately funded World War One in nineteen seventeen.

14
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:33.680
The dollar has lost ninety-six percent of its value since, wars are now continuous and everywhere, and you're living it

15
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.900
right now, reading this sentence with money that's worth four cents on the nineteen thirteen dollar.

16
00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:46.960
How's that working out? The pattern is so consistent it's basically a law of physics: give politicians a money printer,

17
00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.940
they will use it to kill people. Every time. Without exception.

18
00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:55.780
For thousands of years. You invented money to trade chickens more efficiently.

19
00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.250
Within a few centuries, you were using it to incinerate cities.

20
00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:06.140
Remarkable species. nineteen seventy-one: When Nixon Weaponized Money Against You.

21
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:13.220
August fifteenth, nineteen seventy-one. The day your money stopped meaning anything and nobody told you.

22
00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:20.260
Nixon went on T.V. and said, in slightly more presidential language, "Remember how dollars could be exchanged for gold?

23
00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:25.100
We're stopping that. Also, wage and price controls. Also, import taxes."

24
00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:33.700
He called it a "New Economic Policy." On your planet, when someone names a policy the opposite of what it does, something

25
00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:39.720
